@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Evidence-bounded race and atomicity candidate pipeline

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "Typed CPG evidence" as CPG #DBE4FF {
  component "DFG access kind\nField/Index Read/Write" as DFG #D0EBFF
  component "exact Reference\nField or Variable" as REF #D0EBFF
  component "MsgKind\nchannel read/write" as MSG #C5F6FA
  component "LockKind\nacquire/release" as LOCK #C5F6FA
  component "AST parent overlay" as AST #E5DBFF
}

component "iterative evidence machine\nunique site + strand\nsource-ordered locksets" as MACHINE #FFF3BF
component "canonical MHP index\ndeduplicate · no self-pairs" as MHP #FFE8CC
component "per-site sorted locations\nlinear merge" as RACE #FFD8A8
component "per-(strand,location) order\nper-location interferer index" as ATOMIC #FCC2D7
component "RaceCandidate\nexact conflict witness" as ROUT #FFE3E3
component "AtomicityCandidate\nRMW gap witness" as AOUT #FFE3E3

DFG --> MACHINE : typed access
REF --> MACHINE : exact identity
MSG --> MACHINE : channel identity
LOCK --> MACHINE : lock transitions
AST --> MACHINE : lift / group
MHP --> RACE : possible overlap
MHP --> ATOMIC : both endpoints
MACHINE --> RACE : access + locksets
MACHINE --> ATOMIC : access + boundaries
RACE --> ROUT : write and no\nexcluding common lock
ATOMIC --> AOUT : split guard + interferer +\nno continuous exclusion

note right of MACHINE #F1F3F5
  All source-depth state is heap allocated.
  Ambiguity suppresses evidence.
  The CPG is never mutated.
end note

legend right
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF> | typed-evidence container |
|<#D0EBFF> | access and exact identity |
|<#C5F6FA> | typed concurrency metadata |
|<#E5DBFF> | AST topology |
|<#FFF3BF> | explicit heap state machine |
|<#FFE8CC> | normalized relation input |
|<#FFD8A8> | race classifier |
|<#FCC2D7> | atomicity classifier |
|<#FFE3E3> | advisory output |
endlegend
@enduml
